---
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const description =
  'How GlideLingo collects, uses, stores, and shares account, learning, billing, and Google sign-in data.';
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy — GlideLingo" description={description} canonicalPath="/privacy/">
  <SiteHeader />

  <main id="main-content" class="legal-page shell">
    <header class="legal-header">
      <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p>Effective September 2, 2026</p>
    </header>

    <article class="legal-copy">
      <p>
        This policy explains how GlideLingo (“we,” “us,” or “our”) handles information when you use
        the GlideLingo website and applications. GlideLingo does not sell personal information.
      </p>

      <h2>Information we collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Account information:</strong> your account identifier, first name, email address,
          profile image, and sign-in provider details supplied through Clerk or the provider you choose.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Learning information:</strong> language choices, preferences, lesson activity,
          progress, answers, saved learning items, and content you submit to learning features.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Speaking and tutor information:</strong> audio, transcripts, prompts, and limited
          learning context when you choose to use speaking or AI-assisted features.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Subscription information:</strong> plan, purchase status, entitlement, renewal,
          and provider transaction identifiers. GlideLingo does not receive or store your full card number.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Technical information:</strong> app version, device and operating-system details,
          request identifiers, diagnostic events, IP address, and security logs needed to operate and protect the service.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Google sign-in data</h2>
      <p>
        If you choose Google sign-in, GlideLingo receives the basic profile information you approve:
        your Google account identifier, name, email address, and profile image. We use it only to
        authenticate you, create and secure your GlideLingo account, and display your account profile.
        GlideLingo does not request access to your Google Drive, Calendar, contacts, or Gmail, and does
        not use Google user data for advertising.
      </p>

      <h2>How we use information</h2>
      <p>We use information to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>provide sign-in, lessons, learning progress, practice, and account features;</li>
        <li>personalize learning to your selected language, level, and activity;</li>
        <li>process subscriptions and enforce access to paid features;</li>
        <li>operate, troubleshoot, secure, and improve GlideLingo; and</li>
        <li>comply with legal obligations and prevent fraud or misuse.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Service providers</h2>
      <p>
        We share only the information needed for providers to perform services for GlideLingo. Current
        providers may include Clerk for authentication, Google or Apple for sign-in, Google Cloud for
        hosting and storage, RevenueCat and Stripe for subscriptions and payment processing, Cloudflare
        for website delivery, and OpenAI for AI-assisted learning features. Those providers process data
        under their own terms and privacy commitments. We may also disclose information when required by
        law, to protect users or the service, or as part of a business transfer with appropriate safeguards.
      </p>

      <h2>Storage and retention</h2>
      <p>
        Some learning information is stored locally on your device, and account-scoped information may
        be stored in our hosted systems. We keep personal information only as long as needed to provide
        the service, maintain security and billing records, resolve disputes, or meet legal requirements.
        Short-lived billing-event identifiers are scheduled for deletion after 30 days to prevent
        duplicate processing, but cleanup and backup cycles may cause them to remain longer.
      </p>

      <h2>Your choices</h2>
      <p>
        You can stop Google access from your Google Account and manage an active subscription through the
        billing-management link in GlideLingo. To request access, correction, or deletion of account data,
        including help clearing locally stored learning data, email
        <a href="mailto:stefanoscodes26@gmail.com">stefanoscodes26@gmail.com</a>. We may need to verify your
        identity before acting on a request, and some records may be retained where legally required.
      </p>

      <h2>Security</h2>
      <p>
        We use technical and organizational safeguards designed to protect information. No method of
        storage or transmission is completely secure, so we cannot guarantee absolute security.
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>
        GlideLingo is not directed to children under 13. If local law requires a higher age to consent to
        data processing, a parent or guardian must provide any required permission. Contact us if you
        believe a child provided personal information without appropriate permission.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this policy as GlideLingo changes. We will update the effective date and provide
        additional notice when required. Questions can be sent to
        <a href="mailto:stefanoscodes26@gmail.com">stefanoscodes26@gmail.com</a>.
      </p>
    </article>
  </main>

  <SiteFooter />
</BaseLayout>
